sequenceDiagram
    participant AoC as Advent of Code Website
    participant Cache as Local Cache
    participant Parser as Problem Parser
    participant Strategy as Strategy Recommender
    participant Learning as Learning System
    participant LLM as LLM Provider (Ollama)
    participant Executor as Solution Executor
    participant Oracle as Correctness Oracle
    participant Attempts as Attempt Trace

    Note over Cache: Problem Directory Structure:<br/>years/YYYY/dayXX/<br/>- examples/<br/>- input.txt<br/>- problem.txt / problem.html<br/>- answers.json (cached accepted answers)

    alt Cache exists
        Cache->>Parser: Load cached problem.html
    else No cache
        AoC->>Cache: Fetch problem text
        Cache->>Cache: Save HTML & metadata
        Cache->>Parser: Pass HTML
    end

    Parser->>Parser: parse_problem_text() (per-part)
    Parser->>Strategy: Problem characteristics
    Strategy->>Learning: get_recommended_strategies()
    Learning->>Learning: Select top models by role:<br/>1. Primary (generation)<br/>2. Reviewer (optional collaborative improvement)

    Learning->>LLM: Selected models + strategies + effectiveness

    loop For each primary model
        LLM->>LLM: Generate candidate
        Note over LLM: Candidate enters the pool;<br/>correctness is NOT decided here
    end

    alt Weighted consensus reached
        LLM->>Executor: Consensus candidate
    end
    alt Collaborative improvement enabled
        loop For each reviewer model
            LLM->>LLM: Attempt improvement
        end
    end

    loop Candidate execution + repair (bounded)
        Executor->>Oracle: Run candidate; compare output
        Oracle->>Oracle: Judge vs cached accepted answer /<br/>worked example + overfit gate
        Oracle-->>Executor: SOLVED / WRONG / NO_CANDIDATE / ...
        alt Not accepted and repairs remain
            Executor->>LLM: Feedback (expected vs actual)
            LLM->>LLM: improve_solution()
        end
    end

    alt All primary candidates fail
        loop For each fallback model
            Executor->>Oracle: Verify fallback candidate
        end
    end

    Executor->>Attempts: Record each attempt (claimed vs verified)
    Executor->>Learning: Record VERIFIED model performance

    Note over AoC: Answer submission is unwired (submission/ package),<br/>reserved for the solver phase (Milestone F).
